Growe welcomes those who are excited to:

•
Partner with business stakeholders to translate business needs into clear analytical questions, metrics, and data-driven solutions;

•
Conduct end-to-end analysis of revenue performance, customer behavior, funnels, retention, churn, and operational efficiency;

•
Identify trends, anomalies, performance drivers, and growth opportunities, and communicate actionable recommendations to stakeholders;

•
Develop and maintain reliable, reusable data models and datasets using SQL and dbt;

•
Build and improve Tableau dashboards that enable effective performance monitoring and business decision-making;

•
Ensure data accuracy by validating calculations, investigating discrepancies, and monitoring data quality;

•
Take ownership of analytical projects - from requirements gathering and methodology design to implementation and presentation of results;

•
Collaborate with analysts and cross-functional teams, participate in code reviews, maintain documentation, and share knowledge across the analytics function;

•
Support stakeholders with ad hoc analysis while proactively identifying opportunities for deeper, scalable analytical solutions.

We need your professional experience:

•
2+ years in a Data Analyst or BI Analyst, or similar role;

•
Strong SQL skills and experience working with large datasets;

•
Hands-on experience with Tableau;

•
Experience building dashboards, automated reporting, and reusable analytical datasets;

•
Solid understanding of business metrics, data validation, descriptive statistics, and analytical methodologies;

•
Experience conducting end-to-end analysis: from gathering requirements and defining methodology to presenting conclusions and recommendations;

•
Ability to translate business questions into analytical tasks and communicate findings clearly to non-technical stakeholders;

•
Experience with dbt, Git, Python would be an advantage;

•
At least Intermediate level of English (spoken and written).

We appreciate if you have those personal features:

•
Strong analytical and structured thinking;

•
Ownership and the ability to work independently;

•
Proactive approach and genuine curiosity about business processes;

•
Attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy;

•
Ability to communicate complex findings clearly and concisely;

•
Focus on actionable insights and business impact rather than reporting alone;

•
Ability to manage priorities and work effectively with multiple stakeholders;

•
Collaborative mindset, openness to feedback, and willingness to share knowledge.

We are seeking those who align with our core values:

•
GROWE TOGETHER: Our team is our main asset. We work together and support each other to achieve our common goals;

•
DRIVE RESULT OVER PROCESS: We set ambitious, clear, measurable goals in line with our strategy and driving Growe to success;

•
BE READY FOR CHANGE: We see challenges as opportunities to grow and evolve. We adapt today to win tomorrow.
